cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code, simulations, or other research materials in this
  repository, please cite this repository using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >-
  ERCP Timing Before Deterioration in Acute Cholangitis Using Bilirubin
  WBC Creatinine Platelets and Albumin Through a Stochastic Optimal
  Stopping Model
authors:
  - name: Prihantini
abstract: >-
  Research code and supporting materials for a literature-parameterized
  mathematical proof-of-concept investigating candidate ERCP timing in
  acute cholangitis. The model combines nonlinear ordinary differential
  equations for laboratory and latent physiological states, a four-state
  continuous-time Markov chain, competing theoretical decision-cost
  intensities, and finite-horizon optimal stopping. Numerical analyses
  include scenario comparisons, Latin-hypercube sensitivity analysis,
  and stochastic initial-condition perturbations. Model-derived stopping
  times are illustrative computational outputs, not clinically validated
  treatment recommendations.
keywords:
  - acute cholangitis
  - ERCP
  - optimal stopping
  - mathematical modeling
  - ordinary differential equations
  - continuous-time Markov chain
  - uncertainty quantification
